Pet Studio for Visual Studio Code
=================================

This is a personal fan project by Federico Brancasi. It is not an official Microsoft or
Visual Studio Code project, and it is not supported by Microsoft. It works with the VS Code
pet, an experimental feature of Visual Studio Code.

Visual Studio Code, VS Code and the Visual Studio Code icon are trademarks of Microsoft
Corporation. They are used here only to refer to the product the pet lives in.


The VS Code pet artwork
-----------------------

The pet's artwork belongs to Microsoft and is published in the microsoft/vscode repository
under the MIT License reproduced below.

- The original sprite files are not stored in this repository. `python3 -m kit doctor`
  downloads them from microsoft/vscode at the commit pinned in kit/sprites.json:
  https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/tree/9c8b8c2bfda213a859cfd5beffb1c0f2724690ed/src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/browser/widget/media/chatPet
- Several files in this repository are derived from that artwork: the images and animations
  in docs/media/ and moves/*/ (previews and vscode/ sprite sheets), and the pet's body as
  copied into the grids of moves/*/move.txt. Anything you render with the kit is derived from
  it too. Microsoft's copyright and license below apply to that artwork; the changes made in
